PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Core consensus holds: chloroalkane-Cy5 probe covalently labels only pre-existing Lyz:HaloTag-eGFP neutrophils (488 nm eGFP + ~630 nm far-red); mpeg1:SNAPtag-DsRed macrophages unlabeled by exogenous ligand (intrinsic DsRed at 559 nm only). Tail-fin injury: neutrophils first responders (hours), macrophages later. Earliest post-injury signals therefore 488 nm + 630 nm → D. 
Round-1 split: D camp (1,3,4,6,7,10–12,15–18) strengthens with temporal reading of “first” tied to cell recruitment + covalent retention; E camp (2,5,8,9,13,14) continues to claim wash clears far-red and macrophage recruitment dominates. 
Persistent evidence: neutrophil-first immunology + irreversible Halo labeling undisputed. Unresolved: exact FP turnover / probe retention between 48 hpf pulse and 4 dpf imaging; whether any non-specific far-red background survives wash. No new kinetic data appeared.}

